> I'm getting more and more confused as I look at this. As I see it, the logic you're adding already exists in next_timeout(): https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/master/kernel/timeout.c#L79 The calculation of the next timeout to schedule is already being clamped to be no higher than an in-progress timeslice.
> 
> Why is the older code not working? Presumably you should remove it while moving it, but I still don't think I completely understand the fix.

This is clear:
```
			/* timeout  */
			int32_t timeout = next_timeout();
			if (_current_cpu->slice_ticks != timeout) {
				z_clock_set_timeout(timeout, false);
			}
```
Imagine that ` current_cpu->slice_tick` is 10, and the last number of ticks that happened since the last announcement and *now* is 5. The current code will call `z_clock_set_timeout(next_timeout(), false)`. In this case, next_timeout() will return 10 and consequently `z_clock_set_timeout()` will program the timer to 10 ticks from *now*, ignoring that has elapsed 5 ticks since the last announcement  causing the timeslice be bigger than it should.
What we have to do is, if `next_timeout()` == `_current_cpu->slice_ticks` no programming the timer to `_current_cpu->slice_ticks`
